  "title": "FSSAI Challenges Red Bull and Pepsi Over 'Energy Drink' Label Restrictions",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court of India challenges the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) over its order to prohibit the use of 'energy drink' labels for high-caffeine beverages, with companies like Red Bull and Pepsi facing backlash. The dispute highlights ongoing efforts to regulate food-related labels.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court of India has challenged the FSSAI's order to prohibit the use of 'energy drink' labels for high-caffeine beverages",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "FSSAI examined three infant nutrition products and their promotional materials, highlighting issues related to biotin content and promotional language",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Red Bull and Pepsi have threatened to remove the category label, fearing it would damage their brand reputation",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
